## Simplified Workflow (Quick-Reference Checklist)

For generating a plan for a new module (e.g. authenticator), follow
these steps in order:

```
□ 1. Read doc/truong/<module>_functions.txt
      → Note all functions and constants in scope

□ 2. Read the Rust source (src/<module>.rs or src/<module>/*.rs)
      → Understand what each function does

□ 3. Search Spqr/Code/Funs.lean for the module's Lean names
      → Map Rust names → Lean names

□ 4. Search Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean for module axioms/models
      → Record axioms vs. concrete models

□ 5. List Spqr/Specs/<ModuleName>/ recursively
      → Identify which functions have spec files

□ 6. Scan spec files for sorry, axiom, and hypothesis declarations
      → Record all trust assumptions

□ 7. Check aeneas-config.yml for exclude/opaque entries
      → Identify skipped/axiomatised functions

□ 8. Trace import chains in spec files
      → Build dependency DAG

□ 9. (Optional) Search Spqr/Math/ for module-relevant math foundations
      → Record definitions and lemmas used

□ 10. Write doc/fields/Plan_<module>_requirements.md
       → Define mandatory sections and constraints

□ 11. Write doc/fields/Plan_<module>
       → Fill each section using gathered information
       → Follow the section-by-section guide in Phase 3 above
```

